{
  "name": "Guardian Gate - Mega Node Email Workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.chatInput }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an executive assistant that helps users send emails.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n1. Ask the user for recipient, subject, and body if they are not clear. Do NOT invent or guess missing details.\n2. You MUST call the guardian_gate tool BEFORE sending ANY email. Pass actionType as \"email.send\" and include recipient, subject, and body in the payload.\n3. The tool returns a decision (ALLOW, DENY, REQUIRE_APPROVAL, ERROR), an intentRunId, and whether execution was claimed.\n4. In your FINAL response you MUST output ONLY a single JSON object (no markdown, no explanation outside the JSON) so the workflow can route correctly. Use this exact schema:\n\n{\n  \"intentRunId\": \"<string>\",\n  \"decision\": \"<ALLOW|DENY|REQUIRE_APPROVAL|ERROR>\",\n  \"actionType\": \"email.send\",\n  \"recipient\": \"<email address>\",\n  \"subject\": \"<email subject>\",\n  \"body\": \"<email body>\",\n  \"message\": \"<brief message to user>\"\n}\n\n5. If DENY, set decision to DENY and explain in the message. Do not send the email.\n6. If REQUIRE_APPROVAL, set decision to REQUIRE_APPROVAL and tell the user the email is submitted for manager approval.\n7. If ALLOW, set decision to ALLOW and confirm briefly in the message.\n8. If ERROR, set decision to ERROR and explain the error in the message."
        }
      },
      "id": "44a4b92b-7726-4ffd-888d-cfd0b14c4f7c",
      "name": "Email Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [
        -752,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "requester": "n8n-email-agent"
      },
      "id": "c68d3850-6e5e-4738-ab7c-781be20e3535",
      "name": "Guardian Gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-guardian.guardianGate",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -480,
        464
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "guardianApi": {
          "id": "YOUR_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "Guardian account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const output = $json.output || '';\nlet parsed = {};\ntry {\n  const jsonMatch = output.match(/```(?:json)?\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)```/);\n  const jsonString = jsonMatch ? jsonMatch[1].trim() : output.trim();\n  parsed = JSON.parse(jsonString);\n} catch (e) {\n  const looseMatch = output.match(/{[\\s\\S]*}/);\n  if (looseMatch) {\n    try {\n      parsed = JSON.parse(looseMatch[0]);\n    } catch {}\n  }\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    intentRunId: parsed.intentRunId || '',\n    decision: typeof parsed.decision === 'string' ? parsed.decision.toUpperCase() : 'ERROR',\n    actionType: parsed.actionType || '',\n    recipient: parsed.recipient || '',\n    subject: parsed.subject || '',\n    body: parsed.body || '',\n    message: parsed.message || '',\n    rawOutput: output,\n    parseError: !parsed.intentRunId ? 'Could not parse JSON from AI response' : undefined\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "6ee5ff6e-d5e7-41ed-9b7b-9e2694621e37",
      "name": "Parse Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
